---
/* The three motions a machine under niwa actually goes through.
 *
 * Each one opens with the move the reader makes, and each ends at the page
 * that teaches it.
 */
---

<section class="loop" aria-labelledby="loop-title">
  <h2 id="loop-title">The daily loop</h2>
  <ol class="motions">
    <li>
      <span>01</span>
      <div>
        <h3>Change the machine through the config.</h3>
        <p>Add a line, run <code>niwa apply</code>, done.</p>
        <p class="onward"><a href="/start/first-apply">Your first apply</a></p>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li>
      <span>02</span>
      <div>
        <h3>Change the machine directly, then keep it.</h3>
        <p>
          niwa notices, and offers the config line back. Accept it, and your script says what
          your machine says.
        </p>
        <p class="onward"><a href="/concepts/drift">Drift and the write-back loop</a></p>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li>
      <span>03</span>
      <div>
        <h3>Set up a new machine.</h3>
        <p>One command, then read the plan and confirm.</p>
        <p class="onward"><a href="/start/second-machine">Set up a second machine</a></p>
      </div>
    </li>
  </ol>
</section>
